From 85107feb34207ed30705e90341ea5b8c816b7846 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Lane A <lane-a@local.invalid>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 09:30:41 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 09/18] feat(media): add an extended CPU-only transition
 library

Add backend/src/media/transition_library.py, a registry of 248
transition builders across 33 families. Each builder takes two
equal-size clips [a]/[b] and returns one FFmpeg filter-graph fragment
producing [out], given duration, offset, width, height and fps. The
module is standard-library only: no app imports, no external assets,
no GPU.

Most geometric reveals (soft iris, diamond, checkerboard, blinds,
zig-zag, wave, spiral, clock, blocks, barn doors, frame, star,
multi-iris, shutter, corner, pinwheel, polygon, gradient, grid, mosaic,
rings, diagonal blinds) use xfade=transition=custom expressions.
Motion, glitch and light families, plus the blend, strobe, pixel,
mirror, rotate, hue, channel and grade effects, use ordinary filter
graphs (overlay, zoompan, rotate, rgbashift, noise, gblur, blend, eq).

Add tools/transitions-proof/make_library_reel.py, which renders every
registry entry and all 58 built-in xfade names at 1080x1920 with a 0.5 s
join, probes each clip, computes the three-frame grey signature against
every other clip, and writes the honest distinct count, near-identical
groups, render times and contact sheets. It supports --reuse for
incremental registry changes.

Add backend/tests/unit/test_transition_library.py, which renders every
entry at 108x192 / 10 fps through real ffmpeg and pins the join
contract: two cards in, 2*card - duration out, first frame is the
outgoing card and last frame is the incoming one.

